WEBVTT

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:09.010
Looks like no one's around.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.060
Are you... heroes?

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:01.870
Yotsuya-kun and Glen-san 
sure are taking a while.

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:04.790
I hope they get back 
before the sun goes down.

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:09.710
If only I could've gotten Dad to 
tell me exactly where Dan went...

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:12.080
You don't need to worry about that, Jezby.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:16.990
Zagroth was producing fewer and fewer crops.

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:20.420
There was no way we could continue 
to feed all who lived there.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:23.430
If we didn't weed out those who didn't work,

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:26.280
everyone would have eventually 
starved to death.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:29.090
<i>Oh, man. He actually said it.</i>

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:32.250
I'm not asking for your understanding now.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:42.130
Goblins!

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:43.890
Stay back!

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:45.090
Okay!

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:48.200
I won't lose this time!

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:00.440
Seriously?!

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:05.610
Get the kids and the old man out of here.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:06.870
We'll handle this!

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:08.190
R-Right!

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:10.330
We're running away! Follow me!

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:14.160
Iu-chan, I'll be our shield!

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:14.740
Okay!

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:19.080
This side!

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:26.840
Iu-chan, look out!

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:31.020
Congratula.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:33.340
Yes! Rank 10!

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.350
m 0 0 l 125 0 l 125 160 l 0 160

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.350
m 0 0 l 120 0 l 120 160 l 0 160

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.350
m 0 0 l 250 0 l 250 40 l 0 40

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.350
<b>Shindou Iu</b>

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.350
<b>Warrior (Sword)        Rank 10\h\h</b>

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.350
<b>Health\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h> 225%
Upper Body\h\h\h\h\h\h> 195%
Lower Body\h\h\h\h\h\h> 185%
Involuntary\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
Muscle\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h> 175%
Strength\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h> 195%</b>

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.350
<b>•Can use wind magic.</b>

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:35.660
Time for the job roul.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:38.190
<b>Job
Roulette</b>

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:38.190
Gimme something good! And no Wizards!

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:41.070
<b>Elite Warrior (Sword)</b>

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:41.070
<b>Heavy
Warrior
(Sword)</b>

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:41.070
<b>Knight
(Sword)</b>

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:41.060
Bam! Elite Warrior (Sword)!

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:43.570
Hell yeah! An elite job!

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.780
Huh? You changed jobs?

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:52.790
Just leave the rest to me.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:01.290
Iu-chan's amazing!

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:03.410
How is she so far ahead of me?

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:09.210
We should be far enough now...

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:10.800
Great Hero, in front of us!

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:11.640
Huh?

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:17.050
M-My bow...

00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:18.990
Wait, this range is too close!

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:22.430
O-Oh, right! My staff! My staff!

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.580
Majiha...

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:28.120
Fire!

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.190
It wasn't enough...

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:37.350
Huh?

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:42.050
Glen-san?

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:43.710
You okay, Yuka?

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:46.180
Y-Yeah, I think so...

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:47.460
They're over here!

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:50.390
You guys ran pretty far.

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:53.690
Oh, everything's taken care 
of on Shindou-san's side.

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:56.720
Bro?

00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:58.550
Froc!

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:00.450
Bro!

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:03.570
I missed you! I missed you so much!

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:06.700
Froc, thank goodness you're safe.

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:09.260
You're...

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:12.910
Jezby, from the Culas family.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:16.030
Oh, you're Bayne's daughter, Jezby!

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:17.990
Yes, Dan.

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:22.100
It's a miracle that you two have met again.

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:28.390
The people who left on the 
Journey of Hope stayed here?

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:29.250
Yeah.

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:31.900
We heard what happened to the village, Chief.

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:34.460
J-Jaca...

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:37.270
I'm glad to see you're also well.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:39.120
No thanks to you.

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:41.910
Anyway, you must be exhausted.

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:42.940
Come this way.

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:48.320
We don't have much, but help yourselves.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:51.740
I feel like it's been ages 
since I saw real food!

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:55.760
When I lived in the village, I was a cook.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:58.820
I prepare all the food here.

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:00.260
I'll dig right in, then!

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:04.410
You can use this hut and 
the one next door tonight.

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:06.920
We'll be in the ones over there.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.400
I see... So Bayne is...

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:14.950
But everyone from the 
village... and your mother...

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:18.300
The monsters got them... 
right in front of me...

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:24.820
I'm just glad you two and Froc are alive.

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:28.370
Right now, let's just think 
about what to do next.

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:32.670
Speaking of what we need to do next...

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:37.100
Oh, you two are here, too?

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:39.290
If you want food, we'll get you some.

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:40.200
Excuse me?!

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:43.050
Back in the village, you were 
always bowing to Grandpa!

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:44.680
Stop, Iris.

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:45.560
But—

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:49.030
Those of us who were run out 
of the village are alive,

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:53.330
and those who stayed are 
dead. How very ironic.

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:58.330
Indeed. And we were told that we were 
leaving to help our kids and grandkids.

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:05.450
A few weeks ago,

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:08.260
while I was searching for New Eden,

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:10.270
I came across this settlement.

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:13.150
When I thought about the people here,

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:15.850
I couldn't bring myself to leave.

00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:19.260
Before I got here, they didn't 
even have any decent food to eat.

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:21.050
So that meat from before...

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:21.940
Yes.

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:24.430
It was a deer I hunted.

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:28.510
My brother was the best 
hunter in the village.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:31.880
So that's what happened.

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:34.480
And you've been here ever since?

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:37.300
Well, I guess you might say that.

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:40.170
Oh, does that mean our quest is cleared?

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:42.290
You know it doesn't.

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:45.320
We should leave this place
sooner rather than later.

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:46.400
What?

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:48.090
See?

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.980
The monsters that attacked Zagroth

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:54.880
seemed like they possessed 
a will to kill humans.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:59.620
I suspect someone is controlling them.

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:01.870
Who? And why?

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:04.930
I don't know. That's why we're in danger.

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:09.060
I think there's a good chance that 
swarm of monsters will attack here.

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:11.260
How do you know that?

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:13.500
U-Uh...

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:17.550
<b>Stop the destruction of the village of Zagroth.</b>

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:17.550
<b>(Time limit: 30 days)</b>

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:17.550
<b>Quest Time!</b>

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:17.680
<i>It's only been fifteen days 
since this quest started.</i>

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:21.030
That half-faced freak came up with this.

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:24.820
No way in hell he's just gonna be like, 
"Okay, you've finished this que."

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:26.260
It's...

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:28.510
my hero's intuition!

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:29.520
He said it outright!

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:32.450
In that case... we have no choice.

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.400
And he believed it instantly!

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:37.950
So does that mean we 
should head for New Eden?

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:40.630
What is New Eden, anyway?

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.640
A legend that's been passed down 
in the village since ancient times.

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:47.540
It's said that eternal 
peace is guaranteed there.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:52.250
The original goal of the Journey 
of Hope was to search for New Eden,

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:54.840
and young people were chosen for it.

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:56.590
To find New Eden?

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:00.480
Now, it's just an excuse to get rid 
of people seen as troublemakers.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:03.580
There is a continuation 
to the legend of New Eden.

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:06.770
There is? I've never heard of...

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:08.330
Of course not.

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:14.180
It had been handed down in secret only to 
those who inherit the title of village chief.

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:15.610
What's the continuation?

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:23.420
Only those who choose to die 
themselves are led to New Eden.

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:26.440
A place you get to by choosing death...

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:28.340
So it's the afterlife?

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:32.010
You were deceiving the people 
of Zagroth all this time?!

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:33.670
What choice did I have?

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:37.640
I can only keep a poor 
village going for so long.

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:41.390
The village chief has a 
duty to protect Zagroth.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:43.770
Because of that, everyone in the village

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:46.320
was so anxious about when 
they might be chosen

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:49.310
that they lived their 
lives sucking up to you!

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:54.130
But if it still hasn't been found,

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:57.450
doesn't that mean it's really 
just a legend in the end?

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:01.900
New Eden is real!

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:03.970
Jezby?

00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:08.500
I'm sorry... I just remembered something.

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:11.910
Something I heard from my real 
parents before they died.

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:16.610
They said there's a peaceful 
land beyond this forest,

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:18.670
and people live there!

00:10:18.670 --> 00:10:20.330
Is that true, Jezby?!

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:24.280
Well, at any rate, so long as 
those monsters are in Zagroth,

00:10:24.280 --> 00:10:25.900
we can't go back.

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:30.350
We need to find a place where the 
villagers can live permanently...

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:33.150
<i>Or the village of Zagroth 
will be considered destroyed,</i>

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:35.680
<i>and we'll have failed this quest.</i>

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:36.830
Great Heroes!

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:41.610
With all of your help, 
I'm sure we can find it!

00:10:42.230 --> 00:10:43.560
We'll find New Eden!

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:45.600
W-Well...

00:10:46.150 --> 00:10:49.670
In any case, we do need to leave this forest.

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:51.540
Food is scarce,

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.970
and we'll have the elderly 
with us on top of that.

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:56.310
Who knows how long it'll take to get out?

00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:57.740
Also...

00:10:57.740 --> 00:10:59.900
There's a major obstacle along the way.

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:01.620
A goblin settlement.

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:03.540
A goblin settlement?

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:05.970
The surrounding forest is too deep.

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:09.460
We'll have to pass through 
the settlement to get out.

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:11.830
I tried it, but gave up and turned back,

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:13.990
and that's when I reunited 
with the people here.

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:15.810
How many goblins?

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:18.040
At least 30, I'd say.

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:19.980
That's a lot.

00:11:20.350 --> 00:11:22.180
But if it's a settlement...

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:25.660
They'll be gathered in one place, 
which makes a sneak attack easier.

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:27.290
What is it?

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:31.290
I thought I'd borrow a blanket for Iris.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:33.530
Thank you.

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:38.710
I should go get one for her, 
but, well... those folks...

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:40.220
It's all right.

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:47.320
What's the point in showing 
kindness to people like them?

00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:49.620
What?

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:50.220
Nothing.

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:58.020
m 0 0 l 260 0 l 260 170 l 0 170

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:58.020
<b>[Creature Magic 01]</b>

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:58.020
<Can speed up or slow
down the cellular
metabolism of creatures by
touching with the palm>
Can accelerate the target's therapeutic power and heal
wounds more quickly. However, it is not possible to
surpass the individual's own regenerative ability, and
when used, the nutrients essential for metabolism are
consumed from the target's body.

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:10.190
These people are a lot quieter 
than they were yesterday.

00:12:10.520 --> 00:12:12.410
It's like they've changed.

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:13.400
Well...

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:18.270
Wh-What's that?!

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:21.380
A monster's roar! It's the 
one that attacked Zagroth!

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:22.770
What?!

00:12:23.190 --> 00:12:25.260
After hearing that roar...

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:32.720
They can't keep walking any longer.

00:12:33.490 --> 00:12:35.100
I guess you're right.

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:41.330
What? Right now?

00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:43.650
Night would definitely be the 
best time for a sneak attack.

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:48.910
It'll be me, Shindou-san, and Torii, 
with Dan-san along as our guide.

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:51.360
Got it. Don't do anything rash.

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:53.660
Leave it to us.

00:12:54.360 --> 00:12:55.690
Well, we're going now.

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:57.450
Take care of things here.

00:12:57.450 --> 00:13:00.170
Torii the Hero, are you going somewhere?

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:03.310
Nah, I'll be right back. Just wait here.

00:13:03.310 --> 00:13:07.100
This time I'm gonna beat those 
goblins and change jobs.

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:08.590
Change jobs?

00:13:08.590 --> 00:13:12.500
It means I'm gonna come back 
even stronger and cooler!

00:13:16.490 --> 00:13:17.790
I'm surprised, though.

00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:19.050
Huh? Why?

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:21.910
I wouldn't have guessed you liked kids.

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:23.480
Shh! Get down!

00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:29.670
The goblin settlement? 
I've never seen one before.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.320
Wait here, Dan-san.

00:13:31.320 --> 00:13:32.300
Be careful.

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:39.910
Are they guards?

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:44.490
I'll erase my presence with 
creature magic and take them out.

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:46.220
Follow me after that.

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:56.530
Now we'll split up and kill the 
ones sleeping in the nests.

00:13:58.090 --> 00:14:01.000
I don't feel too great about 
doing stuff like this.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.930
Okay, on to the next one.

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:07.100
No one's home? Or no one lives here?

00:14:07.100 --> 00:14:08.000
Keita!

00:14:10.150 --> 00:14:11.060
Behind you!

00:14:12.230 --> 00:14:13.250
Bastard!

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:17.720
Weren't they supposed to be asleep?!

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:19.630
Were the sleeping ones just decoys?

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:21.620
We have no choice but to fight them now!

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:26.300
And that's how we cleared 
the Jiffon Island quest.

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:28.950
You guys went through a lot, huh?

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:30.390
This was very informative.

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:36.250
But... I'm still too scared 
to even kill any monsters.

00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:40.390
Um, Glen-san... 
Remember what you said before?

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:43.350
You try to bear too much 
weight alone, Kusue.

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:45.630
I don't like dead bodies, either.

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:48.780
There was a time when I almost 
became depressed because of it.

00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:50.530
Did you mean...

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:51.580
Yeah.

00:14:51.960 --> 00:14:54.790
My father used to be a soldier in the army.

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:58.720
He was discharged after 
being diagnosed with PTSD.

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:02.480
His mind was so scarred, 
he drowned himself in drink.

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:07.660
Eventually, he started to show me photos 
of the battlefield he fought on.

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:08.840
A battlefield?

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:12.680
Photos of soldiers and 
civilians in tragic states.

00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:15.230
Day after day, he said,

00:15:15.230 --> 00:15:17.830
"I protected this country for all of you.

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:20.690
You're obligated to be grateful to me."

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:23.100
Oh, no...

00:15:23.430 --> 00:15:24.510
So I ran away.

00:15:24.510 --> 00:15:25.670
Ran away?!

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:29.520
I told him I'd never have 
children because I like women,

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:32.330
and he pointed a rifle at me.

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:34.120
That's when I left.

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:39.500
I've been moving all around 
the world ever since.

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:43.670
Is something wrong?

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:44.320
Well...

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:46.750
Grandpa is gone.

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.500
Maybe he went to the bathroom?

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:50.670
Yuka?

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:52.460
It's not time to switch yet...

00:15:54.020 --> 00:15:57.080
Big trouble! Uh, er... ah...

00:15:57.630 --> 00:15:58.600
Um...

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:04.690
I was patrolling and found him lying here.

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:06.850
I tried talking to him, but he was already...

00:16:06.850 --> 00:16:08.720
Who could have done this?

00:16:08.720 --> 00:16:10.890
A single strike to the heart...

00:16:10.890 --> 00:16:13.150
Grandpa! Grandpa!

00:16:13.150 --> 00:16:15.230
Don't, Iris!

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:17.170
No! Grandpa!

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:19.460
I'm going to check on the old folks.

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:21.120
Grandpa!

00:16:21.610 --> 00:16:23.540
The chief was killed?!

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:26.670
The crime was clearly 
committed by human hands.

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:29.980
Are you saying we did it?!

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:32.610
You guys had a grudge against Cox.

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:36.620
It's hard not to suspect you after 
the way you acted toward him.

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:38.580
Y-You must be joking!

00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:40.660
You're right. We have a grudge against him.

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:42.390
Hey! Jaca!

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:45.490
But after being forced out of our settlement,

00:16:45.490 --> 00:16:48.340
we have nothing left but despair.

00:16:48.950 --> 00:16:52.740
What point would there be 
in stabbing the chief now?

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:09.760
A few of them ran away!

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:12.770
Well, we took down their settlement.

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:14.920
Let's head back and bring everyone here.

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:25.130
You have to find who killed Grandpa 
and make them suffer the same fate!

00:17:25.130 --> 00:17:27.240
Yeah, you're right.

00:17:27.490 --> 00:17:31.380
It seems unnatural for Cox to have 
been out there alone so late at night.

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:35.140
I bet he was either taken there 
or called there by someone.

00:17:35.140 --> 00:17:39.060
And everyone here besides us has a motive.

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:43.070
Anyway, we should head to the 
goblin settlement for now.

00:17:43.420 --> 00:17:45.700
Wow, this is remarkable!

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:47.550
Think you can use it?

00:17:47.550 --> 00:17:50.090
Yes. It's so well-maintained.

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:51.940
It's hard to believe monsters lived here.

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:54.630
It'll be worth wielding my knife for us here!

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:58.540
I wish you had just stuck with 
using that knife to cook.

00:17:58.730 --> 00:17:59.640
Huh?

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:04.180
Thank you. We should be 
able to rest a bit here.

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:06.310
We can't relax for long, though.

00:18:07.570 --> 00:18:08.650
What is it?

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:09.600
Nothing.

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:11.630
Magic? Here?

00:18:11.630 --> 00:18:15.020
Any kind works. Just fire 
a lot of it in succession.

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:18.450
Majiha Fire!

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:20.010
Wind!

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:21.860
Is that enough?

00:18:22.360 --> 00:18:24.990
You want us to use up all our MP?

00:18:24.990 --> 00:18:27.150
That's what I want you to check.

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:28.580
Huh?

