00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:31.050
I still have plenty of MP left.

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:33.100
I tested it earlier, too.

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:36.970
When I fought the goblins here 
earlier, I thought, just maybe...

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:39.480
It's just like that place.

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:40.970
What place?

00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:43.130
The place where we met Jezby.

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:52.630
I must hurry.

00:18:55.950 --> 00:18:58.990
Why do I have to babysit?

00:18:58.990 --> 00:19:00.650
I have a great idea!

00:19:00.650 --> 00:19:01.120
Huh?

00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:04.470
When I still lived in Zagroth, 
I saw a flying monster.

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:06.010
We just need that!

00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:10.080
If we find it and fly on it, 
we won't have to walk anymore!

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:11.750
A flying monster?

00:19:12.350 --> 00:19:14.720
Yeah. Someone was riding on it.

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:19.250
Don't believe her. Iris lies all the time.

00:19:19.250 --> 00:19:20.830
What did you say?!

00:19:20.830 --> 00:19:23.370
I believe you, Iris.

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:26.500
Froc, you shouldn't bully girls.

00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:29.080
I-I wasn't bullying...

00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:33.110
I brought everyone here.

00:19:33.530 --> 00:19:34.710
Thank you.

00:19:34.710 --> 00:19:36.520
What did you want to talk to us about?

00:19:36.740 --> 00:19:39.540
I know who killed Cox.

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:43.200
Jaca?

00:19:44.750 --> 00:19:48.390
I had forgotten that he was a cook.

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:51.050
No one could cut flesh without this.

00:19:51.050 --> 00:19:56.960
And aside from our weapons, it's the 
only blade sharp enough to stab someone.

00:19:57.160 --> 00:20:01.390
But couldn't someone have taken 
the knife and used it to kill him?

00:20:01.610 --> 00:20:03.010
He said it himself.

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:03.570
Huh?

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:07.710
What point would there be 
in stabbing the chief now?

00:20:08.050 --> 00:20:13.140
In other words, he knew Cox had been 
stabbed before I told him how he died.

00:20:13.140 --> 00:20:15.400
Is it true, Jaca?

00:20:16.530 --> 00:20:17.850
You...

00:20:20.450 --> 00:20:22.790
You... You!

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:26.040
How dare you?! 
How dare you do that to Grandpa?!

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:26.760
Stop, Iris!

00:20:26.760 --> 00:20:28.760
Iris, calm down!

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:30.660
Let go of me!

00:20:29.550 --> 00:20:30.950
I'll take her.

00:20:31.820 --> 00:20:34.540
Setting aside the details for later...

00:20:34.820 --> 00:20:37.840
Are you all sure you knew nothing about this?

00:20:38.830 --> 00:20:41.680
I'll toss him into the 
nest over there for now.

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:46.720
<i>It's like the old men said.</i>

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:49.970
<i>What point is there in killing him now?</i>

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:02.320
So what do we do now?

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:04.250
We'll just have to leave him.

00:21:04.250 --> 00:21:05.750
Leave him? Here?

00:21:06.230 --> 00:21:08.760
We need to move forward.

00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:10.950
We don't have time to get involved with him.

00:21:11.260 --> 00:21:12.430
But...

00:21:14.300 --> 00:21:19.640
It's true that we're not the police, 
and we don't have the right to judge him.

00:21:19.640 --> 00:21:22.820
But there's one thing that bothers me.

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:24.570
Huh? Iris?

00:21:28.640 --> 00:21:30.520
That's where Jaca is!

00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:31.940
Whoa, whoa, wait a minute!

00:21:32.300 --> 00:21:33.480
What is she trying to do?!

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:34.510
Iris!

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:42.030
Iris...

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:55.040
<b>A Will to Destroy</b>

